From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ThaRae <76752281+ThaRae@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 07:05:50 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Compositor: Anti-alias the edges of scaled images only once

Playing a DrawScaledDecodedImageFrame set an anti-aliased clip to the
destination rect and then drew the image into that same rect with an
anti-aliased paint, so a pixel the image only partly covers had its
coverage applied twice. A pixel 72% covered came out about 52% covered.

Next to each other, such images leave a seam the backdrop shows
through, even with mix-blend-mode: plus-lighter, which Leaflet puts on
its map tiles so their edges add up to an opaque pixel. Every Leaflet
map, OpenStreetMap among them, then draws a grid of light lines over
the map while it zooms.

The draw already stays within the destination rect, so drop the clip.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 Services/Compositor/DisplayListPlayerSkia.cpp |   3 --
 ...scaled-image-tiles-leave-no-seams-ref.html |  16 ++++++++++
 ...ter-scaled-image-tiles-leave-no-seams.html |  28 ++++++++++++++++++
 .../image-transformation-anti-aliasing.png    | Bin 54182 -> 64988 bytes
 4 files changed, 44 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 Tests/LibWeb/Ref/expected/plus-lighter-scaled-image-tiles-leave-no-seams-ref.html
 create mode 100644 Tests/LibWeb/Ref/input/plus-lighter-scaled-image-tiles-leave-no-seams.html

diff --git a/Services/Compositor/DisplayListPlayerSkia.cpp b/Services/Compositor/DisplayListPlayerSkia.cpp
index 00413c20aa22fece538a82d5dffd3d0f90946bc1..29f9bca3d0d33c5a19d51e827c6f1b4ef522da86 100644
--- a/Services/Compositor/DisplayListPlayerSkia.cpp
+++ b/Services/Compositor/DisplayListPlayerSkia.cpp
@@ -464,8 +464,6 @@ void DisplayListPlayerSkia::play_command(DrawScaledDecodedImageFrame const& comm
         if (command.compositing_and_blending_operator != Gfx::CompositingAndBlendingOperator::Normal)
             paint.setBlender(Gfx::to_skia_blender(command.compositing_and_blending_operator));
     }
-    canvas.save();
-    canvas.clipRect(dst_rect, true);
     if (command.isolated_backdrop_color.has_value()) {
         canvas.drawRect(dst_rect, paint);
     } else if (command.src_rect.has_value()) {
@@ -474,7 +472,6 @@ void DisplayListPlayerSkia::play_command(DrawScaledDecodedImageFrame const& comm
     } else {
         canvas.drawImageRect(image.get(), dst_rect, to_skia_sampling_options(command.scaling_mode), &paint);
     }
-    canvas.restore();
 }
 
 void DisplayListPlayerSkia::play_command(DrawRepeatedDecodedImageFrame const& command)
